<main id="top" class="subpage-main">
    <section class="page-header">
        <div class="container">
            <h1>Electrical services for your home</h1>
            <p>Adding a charger, replacing a panel, or planning another job? Tell us what you need. We work in Ann Arbor and throughout Washtenaw County.</p>
            <div class="cta-buttons">
                <a href="/get-help.html" class="btn btn-primary">Tell us what you need</a>
                <a href="tel:7342169437" class="btn btn-secondary">Call (734) 216-9437</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="services-detail">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="service-item">
                <h2>Panel upgrades</h2>
                <p>You may need more power for new equipment, or you may have a problem with your existing panel. We'll check what you have and what you want to add before recommending an upgrade.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Replace damaged or unreliable equipment.</li>
                    <li>Check the electrical capacity before you add a charger, hot tub, or other equipment.</li>
                    <li>Find out why breakers keep tripping.</li>
                    <li>Review a panel concern from your insurer or home inspection.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>A new panel doesn't always mean a larger electrical service. For some EV charging installations, equipment that manages the charging rate can avoid that extra work.</p>
                <a href="/electrical-panel-upgrade.html" class="btn btn-secondary">Read about panel upgrades</a>
            </div>

            <div class="service-item">
                <h2>EV charger installation</h2>
                <p>We install home EV chargers, including Tesla Wall Connectors and other Level 2 chargers. Tell us which vehicle you drive, where you park, and whether you already have a charger.</p>
                <p>We'll check the charger's requirements, the wiring route, and how much power your home can supply. Those details help us work out the installation and the price. We also install outlets for compatible plug-in chargers and handle permits for the work.</p>
                <a href="/ev-charger-installation.html" class="btn btn-secondary">Read about home charging</a>
            </div>

            <div class="service-item">
                <h2>Generators and backup power</h2>
                <p>Start with what you want to keep running when the power goes out. The furnace, refrigerator, sump pump, and air conditioning can need different amounts of power. We'll help you compare two options:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Portable generator connection:</strong> You bring the generator out and start it when you need it. We check the generator and your panel before choosing a compatible connection.</li>
                    <li><strong>Automatic standby generator:</strong> The generator starts and supplies power automatically after an outage. We size the system around the equipment you want it to run.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Bremray is a Generac Aligned Partner.</p>
                <a href="/generators.html" class="btn btn-secondary">Compare generator options</a>
            </div>

            <div class="service-item">
                <h2>Lighting, outlets, and repairs</h2>
                <p>We install lights and ceiling fans, add outlets and circuits, and repair wiring problems. If something stopped working, tell us when it happened and whether anything else lost power.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Add recessed lights, under-cabinet lights, or a ceiling fan.</li>
                    <li>Add or move outlets and switches.</li>
                    <li>Run circuits for kitchen and bathroom updates.</li>
                    <li>Find the cause of flickering lights, dead outlets, or tripping breakers.</li>
                    <li>Correct problems with outlet protection, <a href="/grounding-and-bonding.html">grounding, and bonding</a>.</li>
                    <li>Repair or replace old wiring.</li>
                </ul>
                <a href="/residential-electrical.html" class="btn btn-secondary">See residential electrical work</a>
            </div>

            <div class="service-item">
                <h2>Spas, hot tubs, and saunas</h2>
                <p>We do the electrical work for spas, hot tubs, and saunas. Tell us the model you're installing and where it will go. If you've already bought it, keep the manufacturer's electrical requirements handy.</p>
                <a href="/get-help.html" class="btn btn-secondary">Tell us about the installation</a>
            </div>


            <div class="service-item">
                <h2>Small commercial projects</h2>
                <p>Most of our work is residential. We also do electrical work for small stores and schools. Tell us about the job so we can discuss what you need.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Tell us about your job</h2>
            <p>Choose the kind of work you need, answer a few questions, and leave your contact details. You can type a message instead if that's easier.</p>
            <div class="cta-buttons">
                <a href="/get-help.html" class="btn btn-primary">Start your request</a>
                <a href="tel:7342169437" class="btn btn-secondary">Call (734) 216-9437</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
